## 2. Exponential Backoff and Retry Patterns

### A. `APIClient` -- Exponential Backoff + Circuit Breaker
**File:** `/home/gperry/Documents/GitHub/KNIRV/KNIRV_NETWORK/packages/KNIRVCHAIN/internal/resilience/api_client.go`

Uses `math.Pow(2, attempt)` for exponential backoff, plus a circuit breaker that opens after 5 failures:
```go
for attempt := 0; attempt <= c.retries; attempt++ {
    if attempt > 0 {
        backoffDuration := time.Duration(math.Pow(2, float64(attempt))) * 100 * time.Millisecond
        c.logger.Debugf("Retrying request to %s (attempt %d/%d) after %v", path, attempt, c.retries, backoffDuration)
        select {
        case <-time.After(backoffDuration):
        case <-ctx.Done():
            return fmt.Errorf("request canceled: %w", ctx.Err())
        }
    }
    // ... make request ...
    if attempt < c.retries && (resp.StatusCode == 429 || resp.StatusCode >= 500) {
        continue
    }
}
```
Retry counts: 3 default. Circuit breaker: `cooldownPeriod 30s`, opens at `failures >= 5`.

### B. `DVEClient.doRequest` -- Linear Backoff Retry
**File:** `/home/gperry/Documents/GitHub/KNIRV/KNIRV_NETWORK/packages/KNIRVSERVER/backend/internal/services/dvemanager/dve_client.go`

Multiplies base backoff duration by attempt number:
```go
for attempt = 0; attempt <= dc.maxRetries; attempt++ {
    if attempt > 0 {
        select {
        case <-time.After(dc.backoff * time.Duration(attempt)):
        case <-ctx.Done():
            return nil, ctx.Err()
        }
    }
    // ... make request ...
    if resp.StatusCode >= 500 || resp.StatusCode == http.StatusRequestTimeout {
        resp.Body.Close()
        continue
    }
    if resp.StatusCode >= 200 && resp.StatusCode < 300 { return resp, nil }
}
```
Returns error `"all %d retries failed: ..."` when exhausted.

### C. `InstanceRegistry` -- Quadratic Backoff
**File:** `/home/gperry/Documents/GitHub/KNIRV/KNIRV_NETWORK/packages/KNIRVSERVER/backend/internal/services/dvemanager/instance_registry.go`

